libdatachannel v0.24.5: the C API gathers when told to and reports the DTLS peer's fingerprint

NereusSDR for iOS patch, applied by ios/scripts/vendor-sources.sh libdatachannel
after it copies the pinned archive's files. MPL-2.0, like the files it changes;
the modified include/rtc/rtc.h and src/capi.cpp are published with NereusSDR's
source. iPhone app plan Task 28a (R-IOS-16), 2026-09-27.

The app drives libdatachannel through its C API, which in v0.24.5 lacks two
things the C++ API has and the control connection through the remote access
service needs (the link document, "Control over a data channel"):

- Gathering held until the relay is known. The device's offer goes out in
  introduce before the Core's answer brings the relay credentials, and
  gathering starts only once they are known. The C++ API has
  Configuration::disableAutoGathering and
  PeerConnection::gatherLocalCandidates(additionalIceServers). This adds
  rtcConfiguration.disableAutoGathering (last, so a zeroed configuration
  keeps today's behaviour) and rtcGatherLocalCandidates(pc, turnServers,
  count), which takes the relay servers as "turn:" URLs.
- The certificate the Core presented in DTLS. The device checks the Core's
  identity against the SHA-256 of the certificate the handshake carried,
  never the fingerprint the SDP claims, which arrives through the service.
  The C++ API has PeerConnection::remoteFingerprint(), which the DTLS
  verifier records from the certificate itself. This adds
  rtcGetRemoteFingerprint(pc, buffer, size), "<algorithm> <value>".

Nothing else changes: the new calls wrap the C++ ones as the C API wraps
the rest, and a caller that never sets the new field or calls the new
functions sees v0.24.5's behaviour.

